<title>UK: World natural rubber stocks rose in September.</title>
<headline>World natural rubber stocks rose in September.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>World stocks of natural rubber rose 40,00 tonnes in September 1966 but synthetic stocks remained flat, according to latest statistics from the International Rubber Study Group.</p>
<p>    Data in thousand tonnes -- SEP'96    AUG'96    SEP'95</p>
<p> Natural production		  560	 570	 500</p>
<p> Natural consumption		 520	 490	 500</p>
<p> Natural stocks		    1,650     1,610     1,570</p>
<p> Synthetic production		810	 770	 740</p>
<p> Synthetic consumption	     810	 760	 790</p>
<p> Synthetic stocks		  2,080     2,080     2,030</p>
<p>London Newsrom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
